from pydantic.dataclasses import dataclass", "explanation": "Add the ConfigDict import needed for the Pydantic V2 config replacement. Pydantic V2 docs (migration.md#changes-to-config) say config should be a ConfigDict/dict rather than a class named Config or a plain config class."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/geo.py:9:test-failure"], "search": "class StrictConfig:
    anystr_strip_whitespace = True
    validate_assignment = True


@dataclass(config=StrictConfig)", "replace": "StrictConfig = ConfigDict(
    str_strip_whitespace=True,
    validate_assignment=True,
)


@dataclass(config=StrictConfig)", "explanation": "Replace the class-based config with a ConfigDict, as the V2 deprecation message requires. Also rename anystr_strip_whitespace to str_strip_whitespace, per the 'renamed config settings' list in the migration guide, so the behavior (strip whitespace on str fields, validate on assignment) is preserved."}], "notes": "Only the config-related finding was addressed. The `StrictConfig` name is kept so the decorator line stays the same. Not changed: `__post_init_post_parse__` on Point. It is a Pydantic V1 hook that Pydantic V2 dataclasses do not call, so the range check and title-casing would silently stop running. This is not a deprecated-API warning, and static analysis did not flag it, and it is outside the listed finding, so I left it alone. It needs a human to decide on the correct V2 hook (typically `__post_init__`) and to verify behavior, and tests/test_geo should cover it. The `make_point` function is unaffected."}
